    <item ident="g60fef49c6a1387c9f3bd27dbc26e6692" title="Question 50">
      <itemmetadata>
        <qtimetadata>
          <qtimetadatafield>
            <fieldlabel>question_type</fieldlabel>
            <fieldentry>multiple_choice_question</fieldentry>
          </qtimetadatafield>
          <qtimetadatafield>
            <fieldlabel>points_possible</fieldlabel>
            <fieldentry>1.0</fieldentry>
          </qtimetadatafield>
          <qtimetadatafield>
            <fieldlabel>original_answer_ids</fieldlabel>
            <fieldentry>23395,8522,55983,31411</fieldentry>
          </qtimetadatafield>
        </qtimetadata>
      </itemmetadata>
      <presentation>
        <material>
          <mattext texttype="text/html">&lt;div&gt;&lt;p&gt;What is the difference between a valid emotional appeal and a fallacious emotional appeal?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</mattext>
        </material>
        <response_lid ident="response1" rcardinality="Single">
          <render_choice>
            <response_label ident="23395">
              <material>
                <mattext texttype="text/plain">A valid emotional appeal highlights genuine concerns backed by evidence, while a fallacious emotional appeal manipulates feelings without a substantive argument</mattext>
              </material>
            </response_label>
            <response_label ident="8522">
              <material>
                <mattext texttype="text/plain">A valid emotional appeal uses strong language, while a fallacious emotional appeal uses mild language</mattext>
              </material>
            </response_label>
            <response_label ident="55983">
              <material>
                <mattext texttype="text/plain">A valid emotional appeal appears in formal writing, while a fallacious emotional appeal appears in casual writing</mattext>
              </material>
            </response_label>
            <response_label ident="31411">
              <material>
                <mattext texttype="text/plain">A valid emotional appeal targets adults, while a fallacious emotional appeal targets younger audiences</mattext>
              </material>
            </response_label>
          </render_choice>
        </response_lid>
      </presentation>
      <resprocessing>
        <outcomes>
          <decvar maxvalue="100" minvalue="0" varname="SCORE" vartype="Decimal"/>
        </outcomes>
        <respcondition continue="Yes">
          <conditionvar>
            <varequal respident="response1">8522</varequal>
          </conditionvar>
          <displayfeedback feedbacktype="Response" linkrefid="8522_fb"/>
        </respcondition>
        <respcondition continue="Yes">
          <conditionvar>
            <varequal respident="response1">55983</varequal>
          </conditionvar>
          <displayfeedback feedbacktype="Response" linkrefid="55983_fb"/>
        </respcondition>
        <respcondition continue="Yes">
          <conditionvar>
            <varequal respident="response1">31411</varequal>
          </conditionvar>
          <displayfeedback feedbacktype="Response" linkrefid="31411_fb"/>
        </respcondition>
        <respcondition continue="No">
          <conditionvar>
            <varequal respident="response1">23395</varequal>
          </conditionvar>
          <setvar action="Set" varname="SCORE">100</setvar>
        </respcondition>
      </resprocessing>
      <itemfeedback ident="8522_fb">
        <flow_mat>
          <material>
            <mattext texttype="text/html">&lt;p&gt;The strength of language, the formality of the writing, and the age of the audience do not determine whether an emotional appeal is valid or fallacious. A valid emotional appeal connects feelings to legitimate concerns supported by evidence and reasoning. A fallacious emotional appeal manipulates the audience's feelings without providing any substantive argument—it uses emotion as a substitute for logic rather than as a complement to it.&lt;/p&gt;</mattext>
          </material>
        </flow_mat>
      </itemfeedback>
      <itemfeedback ident="55983_fb">
        <flow_mat>
          <material>
            <mattext texttype="text/html">&lt;p&gt;The strength of language, the formality of the writing, and the age of the audience do not determine whether an emotional appeal is valid or fallacious. A valid emotional appeal connects feelings to legitimate concerns supported by evidence and reasoning. A fallacious emotional appeal manipulates the audience's feelings without providing any substantive argument—it uses emotion as a substitute for logic rather than as a complement to it.&lt;/p&gt;</mattext>
          </material>
        </flow_mat>
      </itemfeedback>
      <itemfeedback ident="31411_fb">
        <flow_mat>
          <material>
            <mattext texttype="text/html">&lt;p&gt;The strength of language, the formality of the writing, and the age of the audience do not determine whether an emotional appeal is valid or fallacious. A valid emotional appeal connects feelings to legitimate concerns supported by evidence and reasoning. A fallacious emotional appeal manipulates the audience's feelings without providing any substantive argument—it uses emotion as a substitute for logic rather than as a complement to it.&lt;/p&gt;</mattext>
          </material>
        </flow_mat>
      </itemfeedback>
    </item>
    <item ident="gecdb4fbfd9273acf4fc5b5f8ac5d8d42" title="Question 6">
      <itemmetadata>
        <qtimetadata>
          <qtimetadatafield>
            <fieldlabel>question_type</fieldlabel>
            <fieldentry>multiple_choice_question</fieldentry>
          </qtimetadatafield>
          <qtimetadatafield>
